# \(X_\pi\)-pulse generation

This directory contains the two pulses used by 1qb-DB:

- Gaussian \(X_\pi\): baseline;
- resonant composite \(X_\pi\): robust candidate.

The experiment supports resonant control only, so the selected pulse has
\(\Delta(t)=0\). A common amplitude error is applied to both quadratures:

$$
H_c(t)=\frac{\Omega_x(t)X+\Omega_y(t)Y}{2},\qquad
(\Omega_x,\Omega_y)\rightarrow(1+\epsilon)(\Omega_x,\Omega_y).
$$

## Robust candidate

The earlier resonant BARQ result is not sufficiently flat over 60 cycles, and
the stronger TTC result requires unsupported detuning. Therefore, the current
candidate was reoptimized directly for the experimental target:

- error grid: \(-3\%\) to \(+3\%\);
- DB range: \(0\) to \(60\) cycles;
- four resonant segments with rotation angles
  \((\pi,\pi,2\pi,\pi)\);
- optimized phases
  \((0,1.822673,5.470164,1.822673)\).

The cost is

$$
\max_\epsilon[1-\min_{0\le n\le60}P_0(n,\epsilon)]
+10\max_\epsilon[1-F_{\rm gate}(\epsilon)].
$$

The first term directly suppresses the DB oscillation. The fidelity term
prevents selecting a pulse that looks flat but no longer implements \(X_\pi\).

## Validation

| pulse | detuning | peak \(T_g\Omega\) | \(P_0(60)\), \(-3\%/+3\%\) | \(\Delta P_0\), \(-3\%/+3\%\) |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| Gaussian | \(0\) | \(7.00\) | \(0.6545/0.6545\) | \(1.000/1.000\) |
| resonant composite | \(0\) | \(31.42\) | \(0.999996/0.999996\) | \(3.85\times10^{-6}/3.85\times10^{-6}\) |
| earlier resonant BARQ | \(0\) | \(22.00\) | \(0.9782/0.8835\) | \(0.0218/0.1165\) |

Here \(\Delta P_0=\max P_0-\min P_0\) over cycles \(0\ldots60\). The composite
pulse uses total rotation area \(5\pi\), so it needs a longer gate or a higher
peak drive than the Gaussian.

## Reuse

Directly usable files are in [`waveforms/`](waveforms/):

- `gaussian_x_pi.csv`;
- `resonant_composite_robust_x_pi.csv`;
- `resonant_composite_robust_params.json`;
- `metadata.json`, including settings, validation, versions, and checksums.

The CSV columns are:

```text
time_over_Tg,Tg_omega_x,Tg_omega_y,Tg_omega_envelope,phase_rad,Tg_delta
```

Regenerate the files from the saved parameters:

```bash
conda run -n curve python \
  proposals/1qb-DB/X_gate_pulse_generation/generate_waveforms.py
```

Add `--reoptimize` only when intentionally searching for new composite phases.
The older BARQ/TTC files remain for comparison and are not selected for this
experiment.
